    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Consequences, dependency and living standards",
      "text": "Population change affects the size and age composition of demand for schools, housing, jobs, healthcare and other services. It can enlarge a market and workforce, while creating pressure if investment or resources do not keep pace. Consequences depend on growth rate, age structure, employment, productivity and distribution. A larger total is not automatically a lower living standard, and a smaller total is not automatically an easier development situation.",
