      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-02",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Young dependants and older dependants commonly refer to age groups outside a chosen working-age band. In the standard teaching convention, young ages are under fifteen, older ages sixty-five or more and working ages fifteen to sixty-four. Use the bands actually stated in a resource. These are age categories. The economically active population is different: it is the people supplying labour, meaning those in work plus those unemployed but looking for and available for work. Some working-age people do not earn, and some older people continue working or provide unpaid support.",
      "claim_ids": [
