      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-03",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The total age dependency ratio is the number in the specified dependent age groups divided by the specified working-age population, multiplied by 100. It is expressed as dependants per 100 working-age people. Do not divide by the whole population or reverse the ratio. The measure summarises age composition; it does not tell how many people each individual worker actually supports or how resources are shared between households.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-2",
