      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-04",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Suppose a population contains 300 people under fifteen, 600 aged fifteen to sixty-four and 100 aged sixty-five or more. The dependent groups total 400. The ratio is 400 divided by 600, multiplied by 100, giving about 66.7 dependants per 100 working-age people. The young ratio is fifty and the older ratio about 16.7, using the same denominator. These are separate components of the total rather than percentages of all residents.",
      "claim_ids": [
