    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The same total dependency ratio can conceal different needs. A population dominated by young dependants may require more schools, maternal and child services and later job creation. One with more older dependants may require different healthcare, care support, accessible housing or pension arrangements. Ageing problems are therefore not simply the problems of an excessive total population. The composition and services needed differ.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-2",
