      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An ageing population can involve a rising older share as fertility falls and survival improves. Older people contribute skills, care, income and community roles, so they should not be treated as having no value. Policy concerns include the balance between support needs and available resources, the design of services and opportunities for participation. A higher older share does not establish the same financial burden in every economy.",
      "claim_ids": [
