    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Standard of living concerns the material conditions and services people can access, including income, housing, food, water and relevant opportunities. Average income is useful but does not describe every household's circumstances. Unequal access can coexist with economic growth. A population analysis should connect changes to the actual service or livelihood measure rather than infer universal welfare from the national total.",
