    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Life expectancy at birth summarises how long a newborn would be expected to live under the current age-specific mortality pattern continuing through life. It is an indicator expressed in years, not a promise about an individual child's lifespan. It can improve with survival conditions, but differences need relevant data and methods. An average does not show all inequalities between groups or places.",
