    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Infant mortality concerns deaths before the first birthday per 1,000 live births in the stated period; formal estimates can be derived through life-table methods. It is not deaths among all children under five and not a percentage of the total population. A simple teaching account with ten infant deaths among 1,000 live births corresponds to ten per 1,000 under its stated complete-record assumptions. Do not substitute all deaths or all residents into that calculation.",
