      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Life expectancy and infant mortality answer different questions, although survival in early life influences broader life-table measures. A lower infant mortality indicator can be a useful improvement without establishing that adult health, income or housing all improved equally. A supported development judgement combines relevant indicators while respecting what each measures. It should not use one health statistic as a complete measure of every dimension of living conditions.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-2",
