    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Rapid growth can increase the number of service users even if use per person stays constant. If a town serves 1,000 people with a given daily requirement and later serves 1,500 at the same rate, total need rises by half. Maintaining access requires appropriate supply, efficiency or other changes. The response should focus on meeting useful needs sustainably rather than treating population numbers as the only adjustable component.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-01-2",
