    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A dependency comparison needs consistent age bands and dates. If one dataset uses sixty as the older threshold and another sixty-five, the ratios are not directly equivalent. Likewise, an age dependency ratio cannot be read as an unemployment rate. Record the groups, numerator, denominator and unit before interpreting the result. This prevents a correct-looking calculation from describing a different measure.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.05-01-2",
