    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-15",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A supported consequence answer therefore identifies the population feature, the service or resource pathway and the conditions affecting the outcome. More young residents can raise school demand; more older residents can change care needs; more working-age residents can create an opportunity if jobs and skills exist. It should recognise contributions and differences rather than describe any age group as simply a burden.",
      "claim_ids": [
