    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The dependency ratio can be checked against the population total. In the 300/600/100 example, dependent ages form 400 of 1,000 people, or 40% of all residents. The dependency ratio is about 66.7 per 100 working-age people because its denominator is 600. Both calculations are correct but describe different measures. Calling the ratio 40 would use the wrong denominator for the named indicator.",
      "claim_ids": [
