    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A demographic ratio is not a household budget. A working-age student may receive support, an older business owner may support others and a child may contribute unpaid work while still needing protection and education. These facts do not make the age indicator useless; they define its limits. It is a broad structural measure used alongside employment, income and service evidence, rather than a literal list of who pays for whom.",
      "claim_ids": [
