    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-18",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A young population's immediate and later needs differ. More children can require school capacity now, while the same cohort later needs secondary education, training and suitable work. A one-time construction project may not follow that changing demand. Planning needs the cohort's size, likely progression and resources to operate services over time. A large school building without staff or materials does not establish adequate education access.",
      "claim_ids": [
