    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-20",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Life expectancy should not be calculated by averaging the ages of people who happened to die in one small sample. It uses a mortality schedule and life-table reasoning. The learner need not construct a full life table here, but should recognise the indicator's meaning and unit. A simple average age at death and life expectancy at birth can differ because their populations and methods differ.",
      "claim_ids": [
