    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-21",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Infant mortality likewise needs the right age limit and denominator. Deaths before age one belong to this indicator; deaths between one and four belong to a different age range. A rate of twenty per 1,000 live births is equivalent to 2% under a simple complete-record interpretation, not twenty per cent. If the question supplies formal estimated probabilities, use the stated method rather than replacing it with an incompatible count calculation.",
      "claim_ids": [
