    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.05-22",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A wider living-standard evaluation can combine water access, housing, income distribution and relevant health indicators. Improvement in one can coexist with weakness in another. More average income may not reach disadvantaged households, while better survival can occur alongside continuing housing pressure. The conclusion should identify the supported change rather than compress every aspect of welfare into one population statistic.",
